(413956, 36224, 2612, '<td valign="top">It''s difficult watching the comments about not seeing the "opps" and not being able to respond. I guess this is one of those situations where I should have looked at the photo more objectively and realized the details I saw while taking the picture would not be obvious to others.<br/> <br/>The boat in the picture is sitting on it''s side in about 3 inches of water. The "opps" is the fact that the owner anchored in shallow water at a time when the river level was dropping rapidly. Once the boat was stranded, the only option was to wait for the water level to rise again.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-09-14 15:50:39.</i></td>', 'It''s difficult watching the comments about not seeing the "opps" and not being able to respond. I guess this is one of those situations where I should have looked at the photo more objectively and realized the details I saw while taking the picture would not be obvious to others. The boat in the picture is sitting on it''s side in about 3 inches of water. The "opps" is the fact that the owner anchored in shallow water at a time when the river level was dropping rapidly. Once the boat was stranded, the only option was to wait for the water level to rise again.', '2003-09-10 01:50:07.000000', '2003-09-14 16:50:39.000000', 0),
