(415083, 35754, 7969, '<td valign="top">Well, i think the idea of it was good (fitting challenge) and the lighting on the words is good also. I guess if I have to be critical about it overall my thought would be, that photography is ''visual'' in a shot that requires  ''reading'' the observer to '' get it''  in some ways to me it loses the essence of ''image''.  Perhaps adding a visual dimension reflecting the words.</td>', 'Well, i think the idea of it was good (fitting challenge) and the lighting on the words is good also. I guess if I have to be critical about it overall my thought would be, that photography is ''visual'' in a shot that requires  ''reading'' the observer to '' get it''  in some ways to me it loses the essence of ''image''.  Perhaps adding a visual dimension reflecting the words.', '2003-09-10 19:14:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(415174, 36222, 2003, '<td valign="top">very nice shot - background &amp; border match very well - only critique would be the lighting reflections -- most interesting to me are the comments so far - this being the week of the "insects" challenge and the broohaha about the spider entries, of the comments you have so far there are 5 that correctly identify the interloper as a rat while 7 misidentify it as a mouse - says something about how we should consider our audience and their perceptive skills when we choose our subjects</td>', 'very nice shot - background & border match very well - only critique would be the lighting reflections -- most interesting to me are the comments so far - this being the week of the "insects" challenge and the broohaha about the spider entries, of the comments you have so far there are 5 that correctly identify the interloper as a rat while 7 misidentify it as a mouse - says something about how we should consider our audience and their perceptive skills when we choose our subjects', '2003-09-10 20:28:50.000000', NULL, 0),
